      "quoted_tweet_id": null,
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Busted! 🚫 These images show a drug boat’s desperate attempt to ditch its illicit cargo. Not this time—thanks to a satellite that detected suspicious activity and triggered the deployment of a @USCG drone.\n\nAs part of our Force Design 2028 transformation, Project Minerva is revolutionizing how we gather, share, and act on information across air, sea, land, and space. With smarter sensors, better connectivity, and integrated data systems, we’re shifting from “patrol and interdict” to “target and interdict.”\n\nContinuing our return on America’s historic investment in the Coast Guard, we are modernizing our capabilities and exploiting technology at every turn to enhance mission execution and support. \n\nLearn more about how Project Minerva is revolutionizing maritime security here: https://t.co/yz1y0IUGet\n\n#uscg #forcedesign2028 #maritimesecurity #innovation\n\n@DHSgov",
      "text_resolved": "Busted! 🚫 These images show a drug boat’s desperate attempt to ditch its illicit cargo. Not this time—thanks to a satellite that detected suspicious activity and triggered the deployment of a @USCG drone.\n\nAs part of our Force Design 2028 transformation, Project Minerva is revolutionizing how we gather, share, and act on information across air, sea, land, and space. With smarter sensors, better connectivity, and integrated data systems, we’re shifting from “patrol and interdict” to “target and interdict.”\n\nContinuing our return on America’s historic investment in the Coast Guard, we are modernizing our capabilities and exploiting technology at every turn to enhance mission execution and support. \n\nLearn more about how Project Minerva is revolutionizing maritime security here: https://www.mycg.uscg.mil/News/Article/4224729/how-new-sensor-technology-is-improving-operational-decisions/\n\n#uscg #forcedesign2028 #maritimesecurity #innovation\n\n@DHSgov",
