      "quoted_tweet_id": null,
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Building the future force! Saturday, @USCG opened its newest recruiting office in Omaha, Nebraska.\n\nAs we modernize our assets and capabilities through historic investment, we are also modernizing how and where we recruit – ensuring we’re reaching the best talent in communities across the country. This office will strengthen our ability to build the most agile, capable, and responsive maritime fighting force.\n\nContinuing our transformation through Force Design 2028, the Coast Guard has recruited over 5,200 new members this year, and expects to meet recruiting goals for the second year in a row.\n\nReady to be part of the Coast Guard of the future? Visit https://t.co/J4bAetd2oX to learn more. #uscg #forcedesign2028 #GoCoastGuard\n\n@GoCoastGuard @DHSgov",
      "text_resolved": "Building the future force! Saturday, @USCG opened its newest recruiting office in Omaha, Nebraska.\n\nAs we modernize our assets and capabilities through historic investment, we are also modernizing how and where we recruit – ensuring we’re reaching the best talent in communities across the country. This office will strengthen our ability to build the most agile, capable, and responsive maritime fighting force.\n\nContinuing our transformation through Force Design 2028, the Coast Guard has recruited over 5,200 new members this year, and expects to meet recruiting goals for the second year in a row.\n\nReady to be part of the Coast Guard of the future? Visit http://GoCoastGuard.com to learn more. #uscg #forcedesign2028 #GoCoastGuard\n\n@GoCoastGuard @DHSgov",
